Fortnite - wikipedia Fortnite Jump to : navigation , search For the battle royale version of the game , see Fortnite Battle Royale . Fortnite European box art Developer ( s ) Epic Games People Can Fly Publisher ( s ) Epic Games Director ( s ) Darren Sugg Artist ( s ) Pete Ellis Composer ( s ) Rom Di Prisco Engine Unreal Engine 4 Platform ( s ) Microsoft Windows macOS PlayStation 4 Xbox One iOS Release 2018 Genre ( s ) Survival Mode ( s ) Single - player , multiplayer Fortnite is a co-op sandbox survival game developed by Epic Games and People Can Fly and published by Epic Games . The game was released as a paid - for early access title for Microsoft Windows , macOS , PlayStation 4 and Xbox One on July 25 , 2017 , with a full free - to - play release expected in 2018 . The retail versions of the game were published by Gearbox Publishing , while online distribution of the PC versions is handled by Epic 's launcher . Fortnite is set in contemporary Earth , where the sudden appearance of a worldwide storm causes 98 % of the world 's population to disappear , and zombie - like creatures rise to attack the remainder .","entities":["Fortnite","Darren Sugg","Pete Ellis","Rom Di Prisco","Unreal Engine 4","Fortnite early access release","Fortnite full free-to-play release","Epic's launcher","worldwide storm","zombie-like creatures","world's population","disappearance of 98% of the world's population","remaining population","Fortnite Battle Royale","People Can Fly"],"facts":["Fortnite -RELATED_TO-> Spike Video Game Awards","Fortnite -RELATED_TO-> missions","Fortnite -RELATED_TO-> Fortnitemares","Fortnite -RELATED_TO-> Storm Shield Defense missions","Fortnite -RELATED_TO-> Unreal 4"]}
