The drawback is the receiver is more complicated , since it must re-create the carrier to recover the signal . Small errors in the detection process greatly affect the pitch of the received signal . As a result , single sideband is not used for music or general broadcast . Single sideband is used for long - range voice communications by ships and aircraft , Citizen 's Band , and amateur radio operators . Lower sideband ( LSB ) is generally used below 9 MHz and USB ( upper sideband ) above 9 MHz . Vestigal sideband transmits the carrier and one complete sideband , but filters out the other sideband . It is a compromise between AM and SSB , enabing simple receivers to be used , but requires almost as much transmitter power as AM . One advantage is only half the bandwidth of an AM signal is used . It can be heard in the transmission of certain radio time signal stations . Vestigial sideband is used for over the air Television Broadcasts both analog and digital .","entities":["Amateur radio operators","Carrier","Signal","AM signal","receiver","detection process","single sideband","general broadcast","long-range voice communications","Citizen's Band","Lower sideband","Upper sideband","Vestigal sideband","sideband","AM"],"facts":["Signal -RELATED_TO-> HF bands","Carrier -RELATED_TO-> Detector","Amateur radio operators -RELATED_TO-> long-distance communication","On-off keying -RELATED_TO-> Carrier","speech -RELATED_TO-> Signal"]}
