This version has been performed by a number of central European ballet companies over the past two decades . Roles and original cast ( edit ) Role Mariinsky 1890 Bolshoi 1899 King Florestan Feliks Krzesiński ( Mathilde Kschessinska 's father ) Queen Giuseppina Cecchetti Princess Aurora , the Sleeping Beauty Carlotta Brianza Lyubov Roslavleva Lilac Fairy Marie Petipa M. Grachevskaya Carabosse Enrico Cecchetti Vasiliy Geltser Prince Désiré Pavel Gerdt Ivan Khlyustin Bluebird Enrico Cecchetti Princess Florine Varvara Nikitina The ballet 's premiere received more favorable accolades than Swan Lake from the press but Tchaikovsky never had the luxury of being able to witness his work become an instant success in theatres outside of Russia . He died in 1893 .","entities":["Tchaikovsky","Bluebird","central European ballet companies","Mariinsky","Bolshoi","The Sleeping Beauty premiere","Feliks Krzesiński","Mathilde Kschessinska","Giuseppina Cecchetti","Lyubov Roslavleva","Marie Petipa","M. Grachevskaya","Enrico Cecchetti","Vasiliy Geltser","Ivan Khlyustin"],"facts":["Tchaikovsky -RELATED_TO-> Imperial Theatre","Tchaikovsky -RELATED_TO-> imperial box","Ivan Vsevolozhsky -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Helgi Tómasson -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Tchaikovsky -RELATED_TO-> Sleeping Beauty"]}
[E92ff9b] {"title":"The Sleeping Beauty (ballet)","text":"The Sleeping Beauty (ballet)
The ballet scenario that Tchaikovsky worked on was based on the Brothers Grimm 's version of Perrault 's work entitled ' Dornröschen ' . In that version , the Princess 's parents ( the King and the Queen ) survived the 100 - year sleep to celebrate the Princess 's wedding to the Prince . However , Vsevolozhsky incorporated Perrault 's other characters from his stories into the ballet , such as Puss in Boots , Little Red Riding Hood , Cinderella , Bluebird , Bluebeard , Ricky of the Tuft and Tom Thumb . Other French fairy tale characters to be featured are Beauty and the Beast , Pretty Goldilocks and The White Cat . Regardless , Tchaikovsky was happy to inform the Director of the Imperial Theatre that he had great pleasure studying the work and had come away with adequate inspiration to do it justice . The choreographer was Marius Petipa , ballet master of the Imperial Ballet , who wrote a very detailed list of instructions as to the musical requirements .","entities":["Tchaikovsky","Sleeping Beauty","Brothers Grimm","Perrault","Dornröschen","Princess","Prince","Vsevolozhsky","Puss in Boots","Little Red Riding Hood","Cinderella","Bluebird","Bluebeard","Ricky of the Tuft","Tom Thumb"],"facts":["Tell Tchaikovsky the News: Rock 'n' Roll, the Labor Question, and the Musicians' Union, 1942 -- 1968 -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Tchaikovsky -RELATED_TO-> imperial box","Ivan Vsevolozhsky -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Helgi Tómasson -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky","Alexander III -RELATED_TO-> Tchaikovsky"]}
[Eccfb42] {"title":"The Sleeping Beauty (ballet)","text":"The Sleeping Beauty (ballet)
The work has become one of the classical repertoire 's most famous ballets . Contents ( hide ) 1 History 1.1 Composition history 1.2 Performance history 2 Roles and original cast 3 Instrumentation 4 Roles 5 Synopsis 6 Structure 7 Versions by other hands 7.1 Piano arrangements 7.2 Aurora 's Wedding by Sergei Diaghilev 8 Trademark controversy 9 References 10 External links 10.1 Video samples 10.2 Scores 10.3 History History ( edit ) Composition history ( edit ) Tchaikovsky was approached by the Director of the Imperial Theatres in St. Petersburg , Ivan Vsevolozhsky on 25 May 1888 about a possible ballet adaptation on the subject of the story of Undine . It was later decided that Charles Perrault 's La Belle au bois dormant would be the story for which Tchaikovsky would compose the music for the ballet . Tchaikovsky did not hesitate to accept the commission , although he was aware that his only previous ballet , Swan Lake , met with little enthusiasm at that stage of his career .","entities":["St. Petersburg","La Belle au bois dormant","Tchaikovsky","Ivan Vsevolozhsky","Imperial Theatres","Undine","The Sleeping Beauty","Charles Perrault","Swan Lake"],"facts":["St. Petersburg -LOCATED_IN-> Florida","Mariinsky Theatre -LOCATED_IN-> St. Petersburg","Willie Rogers -LOCATED_IN-> St. Petersburg","Mariinsky Theatre -LOCATED_IN-> St. Petersburg","five-year anniversary -LOCATED_IN-> St. Petersburg"]}
