We are not aware of any discoveries of lithium , ' he said . '' Lithia ( `` lithium brine '' ) is associated with tin mining areas in Cornwall , England and an evaluation project from 400 - metre deep test boreholes is under consideration . If successful the hot brines will also provide geothermal energy to power the lithium extraction and refining process . Biological ( edit ) Lithium is found in trace amount in numerous plants , plankton , and invertebrates , at concentrations of 69 to 5,760 parts per billion ( ppb ) . In vertebrates the concentration is slightly lower , and nearly all vertebrate tissue and body fluids contain lithium ranging from 21 to 763 ppb . Marine organisms tend to bioaccumulate lithium more than terrestrial organisms . Whether lithium has a physiological role in any of these organisms is unknown . History ( edit ) Johan August Arfwedson is credited with the discovery of lithium in 1817 Petalite ( LiAlSi O ) was discovered in 1800 by the Brazilian chemist and statesman José Bonifácio de Andrada e Silva in a mine on the island of Utö , Sweden .","entities":["Discovery of lithium","Lithia","tin mining areas","geothermal energy","lithium extraction and refining process","plankton","marine organisms","terrestrial organisms","Petalite","José Bonifácio de Andrada e Silva","discovery of Petalite","Utö","Johan August Arfwedson","Lithium","Cornwall"],"facts":["Untersuchung einiger bei der Eisen - Grube von Utö vorkommenden Fossilien und von einem darin gefundenen neuen feuerfesten Alkali -RELATED_TO-> Utö","Johan August Arfwedson -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Detection of lithium while analyzing petalite","Bioaccumulation of lithium by marine organisms in European, American, and Asian coastal zones: microanalytic study using secondary ion emission -RELATED_TO-> marine organisms","Undersökning af några vid Utö Jernmalmsbrott förekommende Fossilier, och af ett deri funnet eget Eldfast Alkali -RELATED_TO-> Utö","Johan August Arfwedson -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Attempts t