The president is further empowered to grant federal pardons and reprieves , and to convene and adjourn either or both houses of Congress under extraordinary circumstances . The president directs the foreign and domestic policies of the United States , and takes an active role in promoting his policy priorities to members of Congress . In addition , as part of the system of checks and balances , Article One of the United States Constitution gives the president the power to sign or veto federal legislation . Since the office of president was established in 1789 , its power has grown substantially , as has the power of the federal government as a whole . Through the Electoral College , the registered voters indirectly elect the president and vice president to a four - year term . This is the only federal election in the United States which is not decided by popular vote . Nine vice presidents became president by virtue of a president 's intra-term death or resignation . The Twenty - second Amendment precludes any United States citizen from being elected president for a third term .","entities":["popular vote","United States","Registered voters","Federal election","Twenty-second Amendment","Presidential pardons and reprieves","Foreign and domestic policies","Establishment of the office of president","Congress","President of the United States","federal legislation","vice president","Electoral College","third term","United States Constitution"],"facts":["Treemap of the popular vote by county -RELATED_TO-> popular vote","Next general election -RELATED_TO-> popular vote","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries","United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America"]}
