Though trained by his uncle Luke Skywalker as a Jedi , he has been seduced to the dark side of the Force by Supreme Leader Snoke and aspires to be as powerful as his grandfather , Darth Vader . Kylo Ren is also the master of the Knights of Ren , as well as a commander and later the supreme leader of the First Order , an organization spawned from the fallen Galactic Empire . He is featured in The Force Awakens media and merchandising and appears in the film 's sequel , Star Wars : The Last Jedi ( 2017 ) . Contents ( hide ) 1 Concept and creation 2 Character 3 Appearances 3.1 Feature films 3.1. 1 The Force Awakens ( 2015 ) 3.1. 2 The Last Jedi ( 2017 ) 3.2 Related works and promotional material 3.3 Novels 4 Reception 5 Family tree 6 References 7 External links Concept and creation ( edit ) After Lucasfilm was acquired by The Walt Disney Company in 2012 , the script for The Force Awakens was written by Lawrence Kasdan , J.J.","entities":["Lawrence Kasdan","Kylo Ren","Luke Skywalker","First Order","Jedi","Galactic Empire","Lucasfilm","Lucasfilm acquisition by The Walt Disney Company","script for The Force Awakens","The Force Awakens","Supreme Leader Snoke","Darth Vader","dark side of the Force","Knights of Ren","Star Wars: The Last Jedi"],"facts":["Kylo Ren -RELATED_TO-> Leia Organa","Kylo Ren -LOCATED_IN-> Jakku","Kylo Ren -RELATED_TO-> light","Kylo Ren -RELATED_TO-> Han Solo","Kylo Ren -RELATED_TO-> Anakin Skywalker"]}
