This process intensified from the 1970s onwards . According to Paul James , `` this consciously created interlock of the image of the multinational corporation with aspects of Australia 's national mythology , has itself over the last decade ( the 1970s to 1980s ) contributed to the maintenance and evolution of those national themes . But paradoxically , during the same period it has reinforced Australia 's international orientation . '' Symbols ( edit ) Main articles : National symbols of Australia and Australian royal symbols Golden Wattle , Australia 's floral emblem and the source of Australia 's national colours , green and gold When the Australian colonies federated on 1 January 1901 , an official competition for a design for an Australian flag was held . The design that was adopted contains the Union Flag in the left corner , symbolising Australia 's historical links to the United Kingdom , the stars of the Southern Cross on the right half of the flag indicating Australia 's geographical location , and the seven - pointed Federation Star in the bottom left representing the six states and the territories of Australia . Other official flags include the Australian Aboriginal Flag , the Torres Strait Islander Flag and the flags of the individual states and territories .","entities":["Union Flag","United Kingdom","Australia","Paul James","Australian flag","Official competition for a design for an Australian flag","Federation of the Australian colonies","Australian colonies","Southern Cross","Federation Star","Six states and the territories of Australia","Australian Aboriginal Flag","Torres Strait Islander Flag","Flags of the individual states and territories","Golden Wattle"],"facts":["Viceroy of India -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag","Chief Commissioners -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag","British officers -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag","Governors -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag","Lieutenant governors -RELATED_TO-> Union Flag"]}
