The 1979 Conservative Budget of Geoffrey Howe cut the small companies ' rate to 40 % , followed by a further cut in the 1982 Budget to 38 % . The Budgets of 1983 -- 1988 saw sharp cuts in both main and small companies ' rates , falling to 35 % and 25 % respectively . Budgets between 1988 and 2001 brought further falls to a 30 % main rate and 19 % small companies ' rates . From April 1983 to March 1997 the small companies ' rate was pegged to the basic rate of income tax . During the 1980s there was briefly a higher rate of tax imposed for capital profits . Chancellor Gordon Brown 's 1999 Budget introduced a 10 % starting rate for profits from £ 0 to £ 10,000 , effective from April 2000 . Marginal relief applied meaning companies with profits of between £ 10,000 and £ 50,000 paid a rate between the starting rate and the small companies ' rate ( 19 % in 2000 ) .","entities":["United Kingdom","corporation tax","income tax","1979 Conservative Budget","Geoffrey Howe","small companies' rate","1982 Budget","main companies' rate","Budgets of 1983 -- 1988","Budgets between 1988 and 2001","basic rate of income tax","Higher rate of tax imposed for capital profits","higher rate of tax","capital profits","1999 Budget"],"facts":["The Guardian -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","First maximum speed limit introduced -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","Traffic sign -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","Metrication in the United Kingdom -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","United Kingdom -LOCATED_IN-> Europe"]}
[E6c7920] {"title":"United Kingdom corporation tax","text":"United Kingdom corporation tax
Another change saw the single main rate of tax split into three . Tax competition between jurisdictions reduced the main corporate tax rate from 28 % in 2008 - 2010 to a flat rate of 20 % as of April 2015 . The UK government faced problems with its corporate tax structure , including European Court of Justice judgements that aspects of it are incompatible with EU treaties . Tax avoidance schemes marketed by the financial sector have also proven an irritant , and been countered by complicated anti-avoidance legislation . The complexity of the corporation tax system is a recognised issue . The Labour government , supported by the Opposition parties , carried through wide - scale reform from the Tax Law Rewrite project , resulting in the Corporation Tax Act 2010 . The tax has slowly been integrating generally accepted accounting practice , with the corporation tax system in various specific areas based directly on the accounting treatment . Total net corporation tax receipts in 2014 - 15 were £ 43.0 billion , which was an increase of 7 % from £ 40.3 billion in 2013 - 14 .","entities":["United Kingdom","UK government","EU treaties","corporate tax structure","financial sector","anti-avoidance legislation","corporation tax system","Labour government","Tax Law Rewrite project","accounting treatment","tax competition","generally accepted accounting practice","tax avoidance schemes","Corporation Tax Act 2010","United Kingdom corporation tax"],"facts":["The Guardian -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","First maximum speed limit introduced -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","Traffic sign -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","Metrication in the United Kingdom -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","United Kingdom -LOCATED_IN-> Europe"]}
[E8d4c78] {"title":"United Kingdom corporation tax","text":"United Kingdom corporation tax
Relief for expenses ( edit ) Most direct expenses are deductible when calculating taxable income and chargeable gains . Notable exceptions include any costs of entertaining clients . Companies with investment business may deduct certain indirect expenses known as `` expenses of management '' when calculating their taxable profits . A similar relief is available for expenses of a life assurance company taxed on the I minus E basis which relate to the company 's basic life assurance and general annuity business . Donations made to charities are also normally deducted in calculating taxable income if made under Gift Aid . Rates and payment ( edit ) The 2007 Budget announced a main rate cut from 30 % to 28 % , effective from April 2008 . At the same time , the small companies ' rate was increased from 19 % to 20 % from April 2007 , 21 % in April 2008 , to stop `` individuals artificially incorporating as small companies to avoid paying their due share of tax , a practice if left unaddressed would cost the rest of the taxpaying population billions of pounds '' . The rate of corporation tax is determined by the financial year , which runs from 1 April to the following 31 March .","entities":["Relief for expenses","2007 Budget","I minus E basis","life assurance company","expenses of management","small companies","main rate cut","small companies' rate increase","United Kingdom corporation tax","Gift Aid","financial year"],"facts":["taxable trading profits -RELATED_TO-> life assurance company","United Kingdom corporation tax -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","life assurance company -RELATED_TO-> profits before tax","life assurance company -RELATED_TO-> group relief","United Kingdom corporation tax -RELATED_TO-> United Kingdom"]}
