In 938 , after the fall of the Tang , the Later Jin ceded the entire northern frontier to the Khitan Liao dynasty , which treated the city as Nanjing , or the `` Southern Capital '' , one of four secondary capitals to complement its `` Supreme Capital '' , Shangjing ( modern Baarin Left Banner in Inner Mongolia ) . Some of the oldest surviving structures in Beijing date to the Liao period , including the Tianning Pagoda . Miaoying Temple and its White Stupa in Dadu which was built by Kublai Khan The Liao fell to the Jurchen Jin dynasty in 1122 , which gave the city to the Song dynasty and then retook it in 1125 during its conquest of northern China . In 1153 , the Jurchen Jin made Beijing their `` Central Capital '' , or Zhongdu . The city was besieged by Genghis Khan 's invading Mongolian army in 1213 and razed to the ground two years later .","entities":["Khitan Liao dynasty","Later Jin","Tang","Jurchen Jin dynasty","Song dynasty","Shangjing","Baarin Left Banner","Tianning Pagoda","White Stupa","Kublai Khan","Genghis Khan","Mongolian army","Cession of the northern frontier","Fall of the Liao dynasty","Transfer of Beijing to the Song dynasty"],"facts":["Economy of the Song dynasty -RELATED_TO-> Song dynasty","Tianning Pagoda -RELATED_TO-> Construction of Tianning Pagoda","Song dynasty -RELATED_TO-> Ming dynasty","national market -RELATED_TO-> Song dynasty","Kublai Khan -RELATED_TO-> Construction of Dadu"]}
