1 Stuarts 2.3. 2 Hanoverians and Windsors 2.4 Commonwealth realms 3 Current rules 3.1 Marriages 3.2 Religion 3.3 Treason 4 Accession 5 See also 6 Notes 7 References 8 Sources 9 External links Current line of succession ( edit ) First six in line from 23 April 2018 1 . The Prince of Wales 2 . The Duke of Cambridge 3 . Prince George of Cambridge 4 . Princess Charlotte of Cambridge 5 . Prince Louis of Cambridge 6 . Prince Henry of Wales No official , complete version of the line of succession is currently maintained . The exact number , in remoter collateral lines , of the persons who would be eligible is uncertain . In 2001 genealogist William Addams Reitwiesner compiled a list of 4,973 living descendants of the Electress Sophia in order of succession , but did so disregarding Roman Catholic status . When updated in January 2011 , the number was more than five thousand .","entities":["Prince Henry of Wales","line of succession","The Duke of Cambridge","Prince George of Cambridge","Prince Louis of Cambridge","William Addams Reitwiesner","Electress Sophia","list of 4,973 living descendants of the Electress Sophia in order of succession","Roman Catholic status","Princess Charlotte of Cambridge","The Prince of Wales"],"facts":["Prince Henry of Wales -RELATED_TO-> Succession to the British throne","Prince Henry of Wales -RELATED_TO-> Prince of Wales","line of succession -RELATED_TO-> Crown","Prince George -RELATED_TO-> line of succession","Princess Charlotte -RELATED_TO-> line of succession"]}
[E480220] {"title":"Succession to the British throne","text":"Succession to the British throne
The first to be affected by the changes , on the day they came into effect in March , were the children of Lady Davina Lewis -- her son Tāne ( born 2012 ) and her daughter Senna ( born 2010 ) -- who were reversed in the order of succession , becoming 29th and 28th in line respectively . Current rules ( edit ) The Bill of Rights and the Act of Settlement ( restated by the Acts of Union ) still govern succession to the throne . They were amended in the United Kingdom by the Succession to the Crown Act 2013 , which was passed mainly `` to make succession to the Crown not depend on gender '' and `` to make provision about Royal Marriages '' ( according to its long title ) , thereby implementing the Perth Agreement in the UK and in those realms that , by their laws , have as their monarch automatically whoever is monarch of the UK . Other realms passed their own legislation . Anyone ineligible to succeed is treated as if they were `` dead '' . That individual 's descendants are not also disqualified , unless they are personally ineligible .","entities":["Crown","United Kingdom","gender","Perth Agreement","Lady Davina Lewis","Tāne","Senna","Acts of Union","Succession to the Crown Act 2013","Royal Marriages","succession","Act of Settlement","Succession to the British throne","Bill of Rights"],"facts":["dark blue flag -RELATED_TO-> Crown","John Lawrence -RELATED_TO-> Crown","line of succession -RELATED_TO-> Crown","2013 Succession to the Crown Act -RELATED_TO-> Crown","Crown -PART_OF-> Jewellery Forms"]}

