[E02bee3] {"title":"It Ain't Me","text":"It Ain't Me
The same synthesizers from the verses are repeated with a piano in the background . Gomez 's vocals in the drop are reduced to syllables from her verses such as a recurring `` whiskey neat '' and are accompanied by percussion instruments . `` It Ai n't Me '' is a breakup song with a theme of nostalgia . The lyrics are about standing up for yourself in the face of a toxic relationship . Gomez narrates the regret of a previous relationship ruined by her former lover 's habits of drinking and partying too often . The lyrics specifically address alcohol abuse , a type of alcoholism . Tamposi explained that `` It Ai n't Me '' is about a woman finding the strength to walk away from a toxic relationship despite the pressure she receives from society to stand by her man . Although the lyrics are sombre , the song has a distinctly uplifting and empowering sound . Release ( edit ) In early February 2017 , `` It Ai n't Me '' was registered on the American Society of Composers , Authors and Publishers ( ASCAP ) database . Gomez first teased the single with two Instagram stories on 3 February 2017 .","entities":["Instagram","alcoholism","It Ain't Me","Tamposi","American Society of Composers, Authors and Publishers","ASCAP database","Registration of It Ain't Me on ASCAP","Gomez teases It Ain't Me","breakup song","nostalgia","toxic relationship","alcohol abuse","drinking","partying","Gomez"],"facts":["comic miming video -RELATED_TO-> Instagram","Maryse Ouellet -RELATED_TO-> Instagram","Mike Mizanin -RELATED_TO-> Instagram","dubmagazine on Instagram: Check out @mikethemiz as featured in the latest issue of DUB Magazine at dubmagazine.com -RELATED_TO-> Instagram","Instagram -RELATED_TO-> Selena Gomez Teases New Music on Instagram -- Is This Her Kygo Collaboration?"]}
[Efaa33d] {"title":"Don't Lose My Number","text":"Don't Lose My Number
Collins has said that he actually wrote most of the song during the recordings for his debut solo album , Face Value . Collins also states that the lyrics were improvised , and that he himself does not fully understand what they mean . Stephen Holden of the New York Times also agreed that the lyrics were very `` vague , sketching the outlines of a melodrama but withholding the full story '' . Music video ( edit ) Collins did not know what he would use as a video theme for `` Do n't Lose My Number '' , so he decided to create a video showing his decision process in selecting a theme for it . In the video , Collins talks to various `` directors '' , who all give him bad ideas for the video . Their suggestions allow Collins to parody several other music videos of the time , including videos by David Lee Roth ( `` California Girls '' ) , Elton John ( `` I 'm Still Standing '' ) , The Police ( `` Every Breath You Take '' ) , and The Cars ( `` You Might Think '' ) , as well as movies such as Mad Max 2 and various samurai movies and Westerns . Track listing ( edit ) 7 `` : Atlantic / 7 - 89536","entities":["Collins","Face Value","Stephen Holden","Don't Lose My Number music video","David Lee Roth","California Girls","I'm Still Standing","Every Breath You Take","The Cars","You Might Think","Mad Max 2","samurai movies","Don't Lose My Number","New York Times","Atlantic"],"facts":["Collins -RELATED_TO-> Atlanta Falcons","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Boredom","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Komarov","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Jack","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Giants release Collins, focus search for backup on O'Donnell"]}
