Unable to reach political accommodation on disputed territory along the 3,225 - kilometre - long Himalayan border , the Chinese launched simultaneous offensives in Ladakh and across the McMahon Line on 20 October 1962 , coinciding with the Cuban Missile Crisis . Chinese troops advanced over Indian forces in both theatres , capturing Rezang la in Chushul in the western theatre , as well as Tawang in the eastern theatre . The war ended when China declared a ceasefire on 20 November 1962 , and simultaneously announced its withdrawal to its claimed ' line of actual control ' . The Sino - Indian War is notable for the harsh mountain conditions under which much of the battle took place , entailing large - scale combat at altitudes of over 4,000 metres ( 14,000 feet ) . The Sino - Indian War was also noted for the non-deployment of the navy or air force by either the Chinese or Indian side .","entities":["China","Himalayan border","Line of Actual Control","Rezang la","ceasefire","Cuban Missile Crisis","Tawang","McMahon Line","Chushul","Chinese troops","Indian forces","Ladakh","Sino-Indian War"],"facts":["China -LOCATED_IN-> Asia","urban-rural type market -LOCATED_IN-> China","Ming dynasty -LOCATED_IN-> China","two fossilized horse bones -LOCATED_IN-> China","China -LOCATED_IN-> World"]}
