Where Have All the Flowers Gone ? - Wikipedia Where Have All the Flowers Gone ? Jump to : navigation , search For the 2008 documentary , see Where Have All the Flowers Gone ? ( film ) . 1960 release on The Rainbow Quest LP , Folkways , FA 2454 , by Pete Seeger Columbia Hall of Fame 45 rpm single release as 13 - 33088 featuring the November 1962 version . August 1965 . `` Where Have All The Flowers Gone ? '' Song Language English Composer ( s ) Pete Seeger Lyricist ( s ) Pete Seeger and Joe Hickerson `` Where Have All the Flowers Gone ? '' is a modern folk - style song . The melody and the first three verses were written by Pete Seeger in 1955 and published in Sing Out ! magazine . Additional verses were added in May 1960 by Joe Hickerson , who turned it into a circular song . Its rhetorical `` where ? '' and meditation on death place the song in the ubi sunt tradition . In 2010 , the New Statesman listed it as one of the `` Top 20 Political Songs '' .","entities":["The Rainbow Quest","Folkways","ubi sunt","New Statesman","Top 20 Political Songs","Where Have All the Flowers Gone? (Columbia Hall of Fame single)","Columbia Hall of Fame","Joe Hickerson","Where Have All the Flowers Gone?","Sing Out!","Pete Seeger"],"facts":["Top 20 Political Songs: Where Have All the Flowers Gone -RELATED_TO-> New Statesman","Joe Hickerson -RELATED_TO-> Bloomington","New Statesman -RELATED_TO-> Top 20 Political Songs","Wilfrid Mellers -RELATED_TO-> New Statesman","Joe Hickerson -PARTICIPATED_IN-> 50th Annual Meeting"]}
