Donald A. Guarisco , also from AllMusic , retrospectively reviewed Faster Than the Speed of Night , and noted the song as an `` epic ballad , '' describing the whole album as `` rock at its most melodramatic . '' Jim Beviglia from American Songwriter said that Tyler 's raspy vocals helped to legitimize the `` melodrama inherent in the lyrics , '' and described the song as a `` garment - rending , chest - beating ( and ) emotionally exhausting ballad '' that suits the throes of a turbulent relationship . Music video ( edit ) Holloway Sanatorium steps , which feature in the video The music video for `` Total Eclipse of the Heart '' was directed by Russell Mulcahy and was filmed on location at the Holloway Sanatorium , a large Victorian Gothic hospital near Virginia Water , Surrey , England . The video features Bonnie Tyler clad in white , dreaming or fantasizing about her students in a boys ' boarding school . Young men are seen dancing and participating in various school activities and singing in a choir .","entities":["Donald A. Guarisco","Jim Beviglia","music video for Total Eclipse of the Heart","Russell Mulcahy","Holloway Sanatorium","Virginia Water","Surrey","boys' boarding school","epic ballad","Faster Than the Speed of Night","Total Eclipse of the Heart","Bonnie Tyler","England","AllMusic","rock"],"facts":["Surrey -LOCATED_IN-> Canada","Dorking -LOCATED_IN-> Surrey","Donald A. Guarisco -CREATED-> Bonnie Tyler -- Faster Than the Speed of Night -- Album Review","Jim Beviglia -CREATED-> Bonnie Tyler, Total Eclipse Of The Heart","Can't Get You Out of My Head -LOCATED_IN-> Surrey"]}
