It marked a departure from their previous guitar - pop based material , instead utilising Chic style guitar - funk and a bubbling Roland TB - 303 synthesiser bassline , becoming the first chart single to feature the instrument . The song also features a snatch of the guitar riff from `` Boredom '' , a song by Buzzcocks that featured on their debut Spiral Scratch EP . The riff chimes briefly in , just as Collins namechecks the song in the lyrics claiming that `` ... and my favourite song is entitled ' Boredom ' . '' Backing vocals on the song were provided by Paul Quinn , the lead singer of fellow Scottish band Bourgie Bourgie , with whom Collins would later record a single in 1984 , a cover of the Velvet Underground song `` Pale Blue Eyes . '' Music video ( edit ) The video opens with the band in a futuristic , but cheaply constructed , control room as they sing , dance and operate various controls . The band then watch themselves on a monitor screen as they walk down a rainy British high street dressed in incongruous , brightly coloured summer clothes .","entities":["Collins","Velvet Underground","Rip It Up","Chic","Boredom","Buzzcocks","Spiral Scratch","Paul Quinn","Bourgie Bourgie","single","Pale Blue Eyes","Roland TB-303","guitar-pop","guitar-funk","Orange Juice"],"facts":["Collins -RELATED_TO-> Atlanta Falcons","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Face Value","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Komarov","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Jack","Collins -RELATED_TO-> Giants release Collins, focus search for backup on O'Donnell"]}
