During the day , four townspeople were killed , including the mayor . Realizing his escape was cut , Brown took nine of his captives and moved into the smaller engine house , which would come to be known as John Brown 's Fort . The raiders blocked entry of the windows and doors and traded sporadic gunfire with surrounding forces . At one point Brown sent out his son , Watson , and Aaron Dwight Stevens with a white flag , but Watson was mortally wounded and Stevens was shot and captured . The raid was rapidly failing . One of Brown 's men , William H. Leeman , panicked and made an attempt to flee by swimming across the Potomac River , but he was shot and fatally injured while doing so . During the intermittent shooting , Brown 's other son , Oliver , was also hit ; he died after a brief period . At around 3 : 00 p.m. a militia company led by Captain E.G. Alburtis arrived by train from Martinsburg , Virginia . Most of the militia members were Baltimore & Ohio Railroad employees . The militia forced the raiders inside the engine house .","entities":["Potomac River","William H. Leeman","E.G. Alburtis","militia company","Martinsburg","Baltimore & Ohio Railroad","engine house","John Brown","Harpers Ferry","Aaron Dwight Stevens","John Brown's raid on Harpers Ferry","Watson","Virginia","Oliver"],"facts":["final assault on the engine house -LOCATED_IN-> engine house","storming of the engine house -LOCATED_IN-> engine house","William Leeman -RELATED_TO-> Potomac River","the bridge across the Potomac River -RELATED_TO-> Potomac River","Capture of Shields Green -LOCATED_IN-> engine house"]}
