, Collinsville , CT ) , in preparation for the raid . The United States Armory was a huge complex of buildings that manufactured small arms for the U.S. Army ( 1801 -- 1861 ) , with an Arsenal ( storehouse ) that was thought to contain 100,000 muskets and rifles at the time . An illustration of Brown trying to persuade abolitionist Frederick Douglass to join him in the raid on Harpers Ferry . Douglass refused . Brown attempted to attract more black recruits . He tried recruiting Frederick Douglass as a liaison officer to the slaves in a meeting held in a quarry at Chambersburg , Pa . It was at this meeting that ex-slave `` Emperor '' Shields Green consented to join with John Brown on his attack on the United States Armory , Green stating to Douglass `` I believe I will go with the old man '' . Douglass declined , indicating to Brown that he believed the raid was a suicide mission . The plan was `` an attack on the federal government '' that `` would array the whole country against us ... You will never get out alive '' , he warned .","entities":["Pennsylvania","U.S. Army","Connecticut","Frederick Douglass","Meeting at Chambersburg","Quarry","Chambersburg","Collinsville","United States Armory","Arsenal","John Brown","Harpers Ferry","Shields Green","John Brown's raid on Harpers Ferry","Federal Government"],"facts":["Pennsylvania -LOCATED_IN-> US","Pennsylvania -LOCATED_IN-> East Coast of the United States","Reading -LOCATED_IN-> Pennsylvania","Sewickley -LOCATED_IN-> Pennsylvania","Pennsylvania -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}

