[Eebc2ef] {"title":"Culture of Australia","text":"Culture of Australia
These wars profoundly affected Australia 's sense of nationhood and a proud military legend developed around the spirit of Australia 's ANZAC troops , who came to symbolise the virtues of mateship , courage and endurance for the nation . The Australian colonies had a period of extensive multi-ethnic immigration during the Australian gold rushes of the latter half of the 19th century , but following Federation in 1901 , the Parliament instigated the White Australia Policy that gave preference to British migrants and ensured that Australia remained a predominantly Anglo - Celtic society until well into the 20th Century . The post-World War II immigration program saw the policy dismantled by successive governments , permitting large numbers of Southern European , and later Asian and Middle Eastern migrants to arrive . The Menzies Government ( 1949 - 1966 ) and Holt Government dismantled the legal barriers to multi-ethnic immigration and by the 1970s , the Whitlam and Fraser Governments were promoting multiculturalism . Countries of birth of Australian estimated resident population , 2006 Some States and Territories of Australia retained discriminatory laws relating to voting rights for Aborigines into the 1960s , at which point full legal equality was established .","entities":["Australian colonies","Australia","courage","nationhood","endurance","White Australia Policy","British migrants","post-World War II immigration program","Southern European migrants","Asian migrants","Middle Eastern migrants","Menzies Government","Holt Government","Whitlam Government","Fraser Government"],"facts":["Australian colonies -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Federation of Australia","United Kingdom -RELATED_TO-> Australian colonies","Australian colonies -LOCATED_IN-> Australian continent","Australian colonies -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Referendums on federation","Australian colonies -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Establishment of democratic parliaments"]}
[E1c6926] {"title":"Culture of Australia","text":"Culture of Australia
Most Aboriginal Australians have a belief system based on the Dreaming , or Dreamtime , which refers both to a time when ancestral spirits created land and culture , and to the knowledge and practices that define individual and community responsibilities and identity . Conflict and reconciliation between indigenous and non-indigenous Australians has been a source of much art and literature in Australia , and ancient Aboriginal artistic styles and iconic inventions such as the boomerang , the didgeridoo and Indigenous Australian music have become symbols of modern Australia . Governor Arthur Phillip hoists the British flag over the new colony at Sydney in 1788 South Australian suffragette Catherine Helen Spence ( 1825 -- 1910 ) . The Australian colonies established democratic parliaments from the 1850s and began to grant women the vote in the 1890s . The arrival of the first British settlers at what is now Sydney in 1788 introduced Western civilisation to the Australian continent .","entities":["Australian continent","Australian colonies","Australia","Dreaming","Conflict and reconciliation between indigenous and non-indigenous Australians","Aboriginal artistic styles","boomerang","Indigenous Australian music","Arthur Phillip","British flag","new colony","Hoisting of the British flag over the new colony","democratic parliaments","Establishment of democratic parliaments","Granting women the vote"],"facts":["Commonwealth of Australia -LOCATED_IN-> Australian continent","United Kingdom -RELATED_TO-> Australian colonies","United Kingdom -RELATED_TO-> Australian continent","Australian colonies -RELATED_TO-> Australian gold rushes","Australian colonies -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Referendums on federation"]}
[E2935ac] {"title":"Culture of Australia","text":"Culture of Australia
They established agricultural industries producing more familiar Western style produce . Queensland and New South Wales became Australia 's main beef cattle producers , while dairy cattle farming is found in the southern states , predominantly in Victoria . Wheat and other grain crops are spread fairly evenly throughout the mainland states . Sugar cane is also a major crop in Queensland and New South Wales . Fruit and vegetables are grown throughout Australia . `` Meat and three veg '' , fish and chips , and the Australian meat pie continue to represent traditional meals for many Australians . The post-World War II multicultural immigration program brought new flavours and influences , with waves of immigrants from Greece , Italy , Vietnam , China , and elsewhere bringing about diversification of the typical diet consumed . Australia 's 11 million square kilometre fishing zone is the third largest in the world and allows for easy access to seafood which significantly influences Australian cuisine . Clean ocean environments produce high quality seafoods .","entities":["Italy","Greece","vegetables","Wheat","Australia","China","Fruit","Southern states","Culture of Australia","beef cattle production","dairy cattle farming","grain crops","mainland states","sugar cane","Meat and three veg"],"facts":["Italy -LOCATED_IN-> Europe","Tour of Italy -LOCATED_IN-> Italy","Deployment to Sicily and Italy -LOCATED_IN-> Italy","332nd Fighter Group -LOCATED_IN-> Italy","Italy -LOCATED_IN-> Europe and North America"]}
