The series is written by Simon Nye , directed by Steve Barron and Roger Goldby , and produced by Christopher Hall . The executive producers are Lee Morris and Sally Woodward Gentle. Lee Durrell , Gerald Durrell 's widow and director of the Durrell Wildlife Conservation Trust , acted as consultant . The series is partly filmed on Corfu and at Ealing Studios in London . Contents ( hide ) 1 Story 2 Characters 3 Series overview 4 Episodes 4.1 Series 1 ( 2016 ) 4.2 Series 2 ( 2017 ) 4.3 Series 3 ( 2018 ) 5 Reception 6 Broadcast 7 See also 8 References 9 External links Story ( edit ) The series begins in 1935 , when Louisa Durrell suddenly announces that she and her four children will move from Bournemouth to the Greek island of Corfu . Her husband has died some years earlier and the family is experiencing financial problems . A Homeric battle ensues as the family adapts to life on the island which , despite a lack of electricity , is cheap and an earthly paradise .","entities":["Lee Morris","Sally Woodward Gentle","Christopher Hall","Lee Durrell","Louisa Durrell","Durrell Wildlife Conservation Trust","Ealing Studios","The Durrells","Steve Barron","Simon Nye","Roger Goldby","Series 3","Gerald Durrell","Series 1","Series 2"],"facts":["The Durrells -LOCATED_IN-> United Kingdom","The Durrells -RELATED_TO-> New Zealand","Keeley Hawes -RELATED_TO-> Louisa Durrell","The Durrells -LOCATED_IN-> Greece","The Durrells -RELATED_TO-> United States"]}
