Appointer Electoral College Term length 4 years Constituting instrument U.S. Constitution Inaugural holder John Adams ( April 21 , 1789 ) Formation March 4 , 1789 ( 229 years ago ) ( 1789 - 03 - 04 ) Succession First Salary $230,700 Website WhiteHouse.gov The Vice President of the United States ( informally referred to as VPOTUS , or Veep ) is a constitutional officer in the legislative branch of the federal government of the United States as the President of the Senate under Article I , Section 3 , Clause 4 , of the United States Constitution , as well as the second highest executive branch officer , after the President of the United States . In accordance with the 25th Amendment , he is the highest - ranking official in the presidential line of succession , and is a statutory member of the National Security Council under the National Security Act of 1947 . As the Senate president , the vice president presides over its deliberations ( or delegates this task to a member of the Senate ) , but is allowed to vote only when it is necessary to break a tie .","entities":["United States","United States Senate","presidential line of succession","President of the United States","federal government of the United States","National Security Council","National Security Act of 1947","President of the Senate","legislative branch","Formation of the Vice President of the United States","John Adams","Electoral College","25th amendment","Vice President of the United States","United States Constitution"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
