This can be used in studies ranging from ecological genetics to anthropology ; For example , DNA evidence is being used to try to identify the Ten Lost Tribes of Israel . Information storage Main article : DNA digital data storage In a paper published in Nature in January 2013 , scientists from the European Bioinformatics Institute and Agilent Technologies proposed a mechanism to use DNA 's ability to code information as a means of digital data storage . The group was able to encode 739 kilobytes of data into DNA code , synthesize the actual DNA , then sequence the DNA and decode the information back to its original form , with a reported 100 % accuracy . The encoded information consisted of text files and audio files . A prior experiment was published in August 2012 . It was conducted by researchers at Harvard University , where the text of a 54,000 - word book was encoded in DNA . Moreover , in living cells , the storage can be turned active by enzymes . Light - gated protein domains fused to DNA processing enzymes are suitable for that task in vitro . Fluorescent exonucleases can transmit the output according to the nucleotide they have read .","entities":["Harvard University","anthropology","ecological genetics","Ten Lost Tribes of Israel","European Bioinformatics Institute","Agilent Technologies","digital data storage","DNA data storage experiment","DNA","Nature","Israel"],"facts":["Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Liberia","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Sierra Leone","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Harvard update on West Africa Ebola outbreak: October 2014","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Early Mesopotamian Urbanism: A new view from the North","Harvard University -RELATED_TO-> Guinea"]}
