Starting in the grasslands of the rift , Homo erectus , the predecessor of modern humans , found an ecological niche as a tool - maker and developed a dependence on it , becoming a `` tool equipped savanna dweller . '' Stone Age in archaeology Beginning of the Stone Age Obsidian projectile point The oldest indirect evidence found of stone tool use is fossilised animal bones with tool marks ; these are 3.4 million years old and were found in the Lower Awash Valley in Ethiopia . Archaeological discoveries in Kenya in 2015 , identifying possibly the oldest known evidence of hominin use of tools to date , have indicated that Kenyanthropus platyops ( a 3.2 to 3.5 - million - year - old Pliocene hominin fossil discovered in Lake Turkana , Kenya in 1999 ) may have been the earliest tool - users known . The oldest stone tools were excavated from the site of Lomekwi 3 in West Turkana , northwestern Kenya , and date to 3.3 million years old .","entities":["Ethiopia","Kenya","Pliocene","modern humans","Obsidian projectile point","stone tool use","fossilised animal bones","Lower Awash Valley","Archaeological discoveries in Kenya","Kenyanthropus platyops","Lake Turkana","archaeology","Lomekwi 3","Homo erectus","stone tools"],"facts":["Ethiopia -LOCATED_IN-> Sub-Saharan Africa","Ethiopia -LOCATED_IN-> Africa","Al-Habash -LOCATED_IN-> Ethiopia","East Sudanese savanna -LOCATED_IN-> Ethiopia","Ethiopia -LOCATED_IN-> East"]}
[E743418] {"title":"Stone Age","text":"Stone Age
The Americas notably did not develop a widespread behavior of smelting Bronze or Iron after the Stone Age period , although the technology existed . Stone tool manufacture continued even after the Stone Age ended in a given area . In Europe and North America , millstones were in use until well into the 20th century , and still are in many parts of the world . Concept of the Stone Age The terms `` Stone Age '' , `` Bronze Age '' , and `` Iron Age '' were never meant to suggest that advancement and time periods in prehistory are only measured by the type of tool material , rather than , for example , social organization , food sources exploited , adaptation to climate , adoption of agriculture , cooking , settlement and religion . Like pottery , the typology of the stone tools combined with the relative sequence of the types in various regions provide a chronological framework for the evolution of man and society . They serve as diagnostics of date , rather than characterizing the people or the society . Lithic analysis is a major and specialised form of archaeological investigation . It involves the measurement of the stone tools to determine their typology , function and the technology involved .","entities":["food sources","technology","religion","The Americas","Bronze Age","Iron Age","the world","millstones","lithic analysis","archaeological investigation","typology","function","social organization","adaptation to climate","cooking"],"facts":["competition -RELATED_TO-> food sources","technology -RELATED_TO-> Macedonia (ancient kingdom)","technology -RELATED_TO-> Crop yield per unit area","technology -RELATED_TO-> team leadership","AllBusiness.com -RELATED_TO-> technology"]}

