Coast Guard Academy , and U.S. Army Herald Trumpets . Coin toss Youth football players from Jacksonville : Tyler Callahan , Tyler Deal , Lawrence McCauley , and Jacob Santana ; New Orleans NFL Junior Player Development coach Tamaris Jackson Halftime show Paul McCartney TV in the United States Network Fox Announcers Joe Buck , Troy Aikman , Cris Collinsworth , Pam Oliver and Chris Myers Nielsen ratings 41.1 ( est. 86 million viewers ) Market share 62 Cost of 30 - second commercial $2.3 million ← XXXVIII Super Bowl XL → Super Bowl XXXIX was an American football game played between the American Football Conference ( AFC ) champion New England Patriots and the National Football Conference ( NFC ) champion Philadelphia Eagles to decide the National Football League ( NFL ) champion for the 2004 season . The Patriots defeated the Eagles by the score of 24 -- 21 . The game was played on February 6 , 2005 , at Alltel Stadium in Jacksonville , Florida , the first time the Super Bowl was played in that city .","entities":["Philadelphia Eagles","National Football League","Florida","Troy Aikman","American Football Conference","National Football Conference","Alltel Stadium","U.S. Army Herald Trumpets","Coast Guard Academy","Paul McCartney","Pam Oliver","Chris Myers","Cris Collinsworth","Tyler Callahan","Tyler Deal"],"facts":["Philadelphia Eagles -LOCATED_IN-> Franklin Field","Philadelphia Eagles -LOCATED_IN-> Pennsylvania","Philadelphia Eagles -LOCATED_IN-> Philadelphia","Philadelphia Eagles -PART_OF-> Phil-Pitt Eagles","Philadelphia Eagles -LOCATED_IN-> Lincoln Financial Field"]}
