Dark Rivers of the Heart - wikipedia Dark Rivers of the Heart Jump to : navigation , search Dark Rivers of the Heart First edition Author Dean Koontz Cover artist Chip Kidd Country United States Language English Genre Suspense , Thriller , Romance Publisher Alfred A. Knopf Publication date Media type Print Pages 487 ISBN 0 - 679 - 42524 - 1 OCLC 45117870 Dark Rivers of the Heart is a novel by Dean Koontz , published in 1994 . Plot ( edit ) Spencer Grant is a man with a tainted , yet shadowy past with a lovable dog , Rocky , who together embark on a quest to find a life in a woman named Valerie Keene , whom he meets in a nightclub . Grant and his dog come back to the club later to find out that the woman is late for work . When Grant attempts to find her at her home , a SWAT - like team bombards the place , sending Grant into confusion . Grant is now determined to find Valerie . He searches for her in Las Vegas and is pursued by a secret government agency who are also looking for Valerie . He gets caught in a storm in the Nevada desert and is injured .","entities":["United States","Thriller","Romance","Rocky","Alfred A. Knopf","Dark Rivers of the Heart","Chip Kidd","Suspense","Spencer Grant","Valerie Keene","SWAT-like team","secret government agency","Nevada desert","Dean Koontz","storm"],"facts":["United States -PART_OF-> Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Northern America","United States -PART_OF-> these ten countries","United States -PART_OF-> The Americas","United States -PART_OF-> Beekeeping by countries"]}
