Faubus argued that if the schools remained integrated there would be an increase in violence . However , in August 1958 , the Federal Courts ruled against the delay of de-segregation , which incited Faubus to call together an Extraordinary Session of the State Legislature on August 26 in order to enact his segregation bills . Claiming that Little Rock had to assert their rights and freedom against the federal decision , in September 1958 , Faubus signed acts that enabled him and the Little Rock School District to close all public schools . Thus , with this bill signed , on Monday September 15 , Faubus ordered the closure of all four public high schools , preventing both black and white students from attending school . Despite Faubus 's decree , the city 's population had the chance of refuting the bill since the school - closing law necessitated a referendum . The referendum , which would either condone or condemn Faubus 's law , was to take place within thirty days . A week before the referendum , which was scheduled to take place on September 27 , Faubus addressed the citizens of Little Rock in an attempt to secure their votes .","entities":["Little Rock Nine","Little Rock School District","Faubus","Federal Courts","Federal Courts ruling against the delay of de-segregation","de-segregation","Extraordinary Session of the State Legislature","segregation bills","Signing of acts enabling school closures","school-closing law","Closure of all four public high schools","Faubus addressed the citizens of Little Rock","referendum","Little Rock","State legislature"],"facts":["Little Rock Nine -RELATED_TO-> Little Rock Central High","Little Rock Nine -RELATED_TO-> Little Rock","Little Rock Nine -RELATED_TO-> The Oprah Winfrey Show","Little Rock Nine -RELATED_TO-> Père Marquette Discovery Award","Little Rock Nine -RELATED_TO-> Little Rock Central High School"]}
