During the 19th century , these crimes saw about 80 people hanged each year throughout Australia . Before and after federation , each state made its own criminal laws and punishments . For a full list see : Main article : List of people legally executed in Australia Commonwealth ( edit ) In 1973 the Death Penalty Abolition Act 1973 of the Commonwealth abolished the death penalty for federal offences . It provided in Section 3 that the Act applied to any offence against a law of the Commonwealth , the Territories or under an Imperial Act , and in s . 4 that `` ( a ) person is not liable to the punishment of death for any offence '' . No executions were carried out under the bridge of the federal government and the passage of the Death Penalty Abolition Act 1973 saw the death penalty replaced with life imprisonment as their maximum punishment . Since the Commonwealth effects of utilising this Act no more individuals have been exposed to the death penalty and it is now replaced with life imprisonment . On 11 March 2010 Federal Parliament passed laws that prevent the death penalty from being reintroduced by any state or territory in Australia .","entities":["Commonwealth","territories","federal parliament","Australia","life imprisonment","Capital punishment in Australia","Death Penalty Abolition Act 1973","federal offences","Imperial Act","Federal Parliament passed laws that prevent the death penalty from being reintroduced","List of people legally executed in Australia","death penalty"],"facts":["Referendums on federation -RELATED_TO-> Commonwealth","Kenya -RELATED_TO-> Commonwealth","proclamation of accession of Elizabeth II -RELATED_TO-> Commonwealth","South Africa joined the Commonwealth -RELATED_TO-> Commonwealth","qualification system of the Commonwealth -RELATED_TO-> Commonwealth"]}
