Career ( edit ) The 1960s ( edit ) After his 16 weeks at Sunbeam Music were up , he was not rehired and then began writing and singing his own songs for demo purposes . `` I never really chose songwriting , '' he says . `` It just absorbed me and became more and more important in my life . '' Diamond 's first recording contract was billed as `` Neil and Jack '' , an Everly Brothers - type duo comprising Diamond and high school friend Jack Parker . They recorded two unsuccessful singles : `` You Are My Love at Last '' b / w `` What Will I Do '' and `` I 'm Afraid '' b / w `` Till You 've Tried Love '' , both released in 1962 . Later in 1962 , Diamond signed with the Columbia Records label as a solo performer . Columbia released the single `` At Night '' b / w `` Clown Town '' in July 1963 , which Billboard gave an excellent review , but it still failed to chart . Columbia dropped him from their label and he was back to writing songs , in and out of publishing houses for the next seven years .","entities":["Billboard","Sunbeam Music","Jack Parker","Neil and Jack","Everly Brothers","Columbia Records","You Are My Love at Last b/w What Will I Do","I'm Afraid b/w Till You've Tried Love","At Night b/w Clown Town","Neil Diamond"],"facts":["Billboard -LOCATED_IN-> New York","Billboard -RELATED_TO-> 'Total Eclipse of the Heart' Sales Rise More Than 500 %","Billboard -RELATED_TO-> Three Dog Night Chart History (Hot 100)","Billboard -RELATED_TO-> Prometheus Global Media","Billboard -LOCATED_IN-> US"]}
