to 10 : 00 a.m. Eastern Time in several Southern and Midwestern states via syndication through Premiere Networks , primarily airing on classic rock , active rock , and country stations . The format consists of talk segments intermixed with music , contests , and skit - based humor . Current events , right - wing politics , sports ( mainly NASCAR ) , and male - oriented problems are common topics of talk . Broadcast states include North Carolina , Alabama , Arkansas , Florida , Georgia , Illinois , Indiana , Iowa , Kansas , Kentucky , Louisiana , Maryland , Michigan , Mississippi , Missouri , New Jersey , South Carolina , Tennessee , Texas , Ohio , Pennsylvania , Virginia , and West Virginia . The duo frequently interviews musicians , comedians , NASCAR drivers , professional wrestlers , and other public figures , such as Robert Earl Keen , Killer Beaz , Manny Pacquiao , Stephen Curry , Rodney Carrington , James Gregory , Pat McCrory and the late Tim Wilson . The show also markets a line of Bar - B - Que sauces ( named John Boy & Billy Grillin ' Sauce ) .","entities":["Talk","Missouri","Pennsylvania","Ohio","New Jersey","Florida","Kansas","country","Active rock","Classic rock","Alabama","Indiana","Kentucky","Louisiana","Texas"],"facts":["The John Boy & Billy Big Show -RELATED_TO-> Talk","Pirate radio broadcasters -RELATED_TO-> Talk","Missouri -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Missouri -LOCATED_IN-> US","Missouri -LOCATED_IN-> Midwestern United States"]}
