and played `` The Boys Are Back in Town '' by Thin Lizzy . One difference on the new station , said John Boy , was `` We 'll actually listen to the music ... we 're rock ' n ' roll guys . '' John Boy was arrested at a night club October 21 , 1990 , and charged with felony possession of marijuana , but the charge was later reduced to a misdemeanor because the amount was small . As part of his plea agreement , John Boy agreed to broadcast anti-drug messages on WRFX . Early in 1993 , news came out that John Boy and Billy were being asked by Mel Karmazin ( boss to Howard Stern ) to move to Atlanta , Georgia , and syndicate their show . At the time , WROQ in Greenville , South Carolina , was the only other station carrying the show . WRFX general manager Jack Daniel said the station made a six - year deal that would keep John Boy and Billy at WRFX but also allow the show to be heard in Atlanta , along with Raleigh and Columbia in the Carolinas as well as Texas , with the hosts getting a share of syndication income .","entities":["Raleigh","Texas","Atlanta","South Carolina","Greenville","Columbia","Howard Stern","Billy","Thin Lizzy","The Boys Are Back in Town","John Boy","WRFX","Mel Karmazin","WROQ","Jack Daniel"],"facts":["Raleigh -LOCATED_IN-> North Carolina","Raleigh -LOCATED_IN-> United States","RBC Center -LOCATED_IN-> Raleigh","tag team match -LOCATED_IN-> Raleigh","WZZU -LOCATED_IN-> Raleigh"]}
