It is not unheard of for Mexican Americans to serve their turkey with mole and roasted corn . In Puerto Rico , the Thanksgiving meal is completed with arroz con gandules ( rice with pigeon peas ) or arroz con maiz ( rice with corn ) , pasteles ( root tamales ) stuffed with turkey , pumpkin - coconut crème caramel , corn bread with longaniza , potato salad , roasted white sweet potatoes and Spanish sparkling hard cider . Turkey in Puerto Rico is stuffed with mofongo . Cuban - Americans traditionally serve the turkey alongside a small roasted pork and include white rice and black beans or kidney beans . Vegetarians or vegans have been known to serve alternative entree centerpieces such as a large vegetable pie or a stuffed and baked pumpkin or tofu substitutes . Many Midwesterners ( such as Minnesotans ) of Norwegian or Scandinavian descent set the table with lefse . Beverages ( edit ) The beverages at Thanksgiving can vary as much as the side dishes , often depending on who is present at the table and their tastes . Spirits or cocktails sometimes may be served before the main meal .","entities":["mole","Puerto Rico","spirits","Beverages","Norwegian","Thanksgiving dinner","turkey","Mexican Americans","roasted corn","arroz con gandules","arroz con maiz","pasteles","pumpkin-coconut crème caramel","corn bread with longaniza","potato salad"],"facts":["mole -RELATED_TO-> bones","Puerto Rico -LOCATED_IN-> United States","Puerto Rico -LOCATED_IN-> North America","Puerto Rico's sugar industry -LOCATED_IN-> Puerto Rico","Two hurricanes -LOCATED_IN-> Puerto Rico"]}
